import AxQM.Core.FourGateReversibleWireTower
import AxQM.Core.PlacedMultiControlledX
import AxQM.Postulates.API.ControlledControlledUnitary

/-!
# The reachable reversible gate cores, over the named gates `CNOT, Toffoli`
(N&C Exercise 4.43, named-gate re-expression of the reversible family)

The universality argument of Exercise 4.43 shows the **operator density on the control tower**
(`exists_phase_smul_op_mem_closure_op_reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions`,
`AxQM/Postulates/API/FourGateReachableTowerDensity.lean`): up to a global phase every tower
evolution is a limit of the operators of the tower circuit submonoid
`reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions n θ` (`AxQM/Core/FourGateReachableCircuitTower.lean`). That
submonoid is generated by two families of gates:

* the single-tower-wire reachable single-qubit rotations `Evolution.qtowerSingleWire n i E`
  (`E ∈ reachableRotationGates θ`), and
* the `≤ 2`-control reversible tower gates `mcNotTowerGate n S t ht` (`|S| ≤ 2`).

For the *named* four-gate universality conclusion, these gates must be re-expressed
over the four **named** gates `hadamardGate, sGate, cnotGate, toffoliGate`.
`AxQM/Core/FourGateNamedRotationTower.lean` does this for the **rotation** family (with
`hadamardGate`, `sGate`). **This file does it for the reversible
family**: it identifies the multiply-controlled `NOT` blocks `Cᵏ(X)` that the reversible
gates are built from — for the reachable range `k = |S| ≤ 2` — with the named gates
`NOT = pauliXGate`, `CNOT = cnotGate`, `Toffoli = toffoliGate`.

## The core of a reversible gate is the named gate

Each reversible gate `mcNotTowerGate n S t ht` (`AxQM/Core/FourGateReversibleWireTower.lean`) is
the `placedMcNot S t ht` gate transported onto the tower, and `placedMcNot`
(`AxQM/Core/McNotCircuitEvolution.lean`) places the arity-indexed block
`Evolution.placedMcCtrlX (S.card) …` — the `Cᵏ(X)` gate on `k = |S|` controls — onto the wires
`(S, t)`. That block is
`Evolution.placedMcCtrlX k b σ = (Evolution.tensorPowMcCtrlX k).onWires b σ`
(`AxQM/Core/PlacedMultiControlledX.lean`), and the symmetric-register `Cᵏ(X)` gate itself is
`Evolution.tensorPowMcCtrlX k = Evolution.congr (qtowerQubitTensorPow k) (mcCtrl k pauliXGate)`
(`AxQM/Core/TensorPowMultiControlledX.lean`). So the *core* of every reversible gate, before any
wire placement or register transport, is the multiply-controlled `NOT` `mcCtrl k pauliXGate`. For
the reachable range `k = |S| ≤ 2` this core **is** one of the three named reversible gates.

## What is formalised

* `mcCtrl_one_pauliXGate_eq_cnotGate`, `mcCtrl_two_pauliXGate_eq_toffoliGate` — **the root
  identifications.** The multiply-controlled `NOT` core is the named `CNOT`/`Toffoli`:

    `mcCtrl 1 pauliXGate = cnotGate`,   `mcCtrl 2 pauliXGate = toffoliGate`.

  (`k = 0` is `mcCtrl 0 pauliXGate = pauliXGate`, the base case `mcCtrl_zero`.) Immediate from the
  `mcCtrl` recursion `mcCtrl (k+1) E = controlledUnitary (mcCtrl k E)`
  (`mcCtrl_succ` / `mcCtrl_zero`) and the named-gate definitions
  `cnotGate = controlledUnitary pauliXGate` (`cnotGate_def`) /
  `toffoliGate = ccontrolledUnitary pauliXGate = controlledUnitary (controlledUnitary pauliXGate)`.
  These are the reversible counterpart of the rotation half's
  `reachableRotationGates_le_closure_named`, which does the same for `H`/`S`.
* `tensorPowMcCtrlX_zero_eq_congr_pauliXGate`, `tensorPowMcCtrlX_one_eq_congr_cnotGate`,
  `tensorPowMcCtrlX_two_eq_congr_toffoliGate` — **the symmetric-register `Cᵏ(X)` block is the
  named gate.** Transporting the root identification along the tower ↔ tensor-power bridge
  `qtowerQubitTensorPow k`:

    `Evolution.tensorPowMcCtrlX k = Evolution.congr (qtowerQubitTensorPow k) <named gate>`

  for the three named gates at `k = 0, 1, 2`. This is the `Cᵏ(X)` block on the symmetric
  `(k+1)`-fold power the wire placement `Evolution.onWires` consumes.
* `placedMcCtrlX_zero_eq_onWires_pauliXGate`, `placedMcCtrlX_one_eq_onWires_cnotGate`,
  `placedMcCtrlX_two_eq_onWires_toffoliGate` — **the wire-placed `Cᵏ(X)` block is the named gate
  placed on wires.** The exact form `placedMcNot` (hence every reversible gate
  `mcNotTowerGate`) uses:

    `Evolution.placedMcCtrlX k b σ`
      `= (Evolution.congr (qtowerQubitTensorPow k) <named gate>).onWires b σ`

  for `k = 0, 1, 2` — the wire-addressed `NOT`/`CNOT`/`Toffoli`. So every reversible gate of
  `reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions n θ`, for `|S| ≤ 2`, has as its placed core exactly one of the
  four named gates `pauliXGate` / `cnotGate` / `toffoliGate` (the `NOT = pauliXGate` being itself an
  `{H, S}` circuit, `pauliXGate_eq_hadamardGate_sGateSq`, already inside the named rotation gate
  set), placed on the wire set `(S, t)`.
-/

namespace AxQM

noncomputable section

/-- **The single-control `NOT` core is the named `CNOT`.** The one-controlled multiply-controlled
`NOT` `mcCtrl 1 pauliXGate` (on `qtower 1 qubit = qubit ⊗ qubit`) is the named CNOT gate
`cnotGate`. Immediate from the `mcCtrl` recursion
`mcCtrl 1 E = controlledUnitary (mcCtrl 0 E) = controlledUnitary E` (`mcCtrl_succ` / `mcCtrl_zero`)
and `cnotGate = controlledUnitary pauliXGate` (`cnotGate_def`). -/
theorem mcCtrl_one_pauliXGate_eq_cnotGate : mcCtrl 1 pauliXGate = cnotGate := by
  rw [mcCtrl_succ, mcCtrl_zero]; rfl

/-- **The two-control `NOT` core is the named `Toffoli`.** The two-controlled multiply-controlled
`NOT` `mcCtrl 2 pauliXGate` (on `qtower 2 qubit = qubit ⊗ (qubit ⊗ qubit)`) is the named Toffoli
gate `toffoliGate`. Immediate from iterating the `mcCtrl` recursion to
`controlledUnitary (controlledUnitary pauliXGate)` (`mcCtrl_succ` twice, `mcCtrl_zero`) and
`toffoliGate = ccontrolledUnitary pauliXGate = controlledUnitary (controlledUnitary pauliXGate)`. -/
theorem mcCtrl_two_pauliXGate_eq_toffoliGate : mcCtrl 2 pauliXGate = toffoliGate := by
  rw [mcCtrl_succ, mcCtrl_succ, mcCtrl_zero]; rfl

/-- **The symmetric-register `C⁰(X)` block is the named `NOT`.** The zero-control block
`Evolution.tensorPowMcCtrlX 0` on `qubit ^⊗ₛ 1` is the named Pauli-`X` gate transported along
the tower ↔ tensor-power bridge:
`tensorPowMcCtrlX 0 = Evolution.congr (qtowerQubitTensorPow 0) pauliXGate`.
From `tensorPowMcCtrlX_def` and `mcCtrl_zero`. -/
theorem tensorPowMcCtrlX_zero_eq_congr_pauliXGate :
    Evolution.tensorPowMcCtrlX 0 = Evolution.congr (qtowerQubitTensorPow 0) pauliXGate := by
  rw [Evolution.tensorPowMcCtrlX_def, mcCtrl_zero]

/-- **The symmetric-register `C¹(X)` block is the named `CNOT`.** The one-control block
`Evolution.tensorPowMcCtrlX 1` on `qubit ^⊗ₛ 2` is the named CNOT gate transported along the
tower ↔ tensor-power bridge:
`tensorPowMcCtrlX 1 = Evolution.congr (qtowerQubitTensorPow 1) cnotGate`.
From `tensorPowMcCtrlX_def` and `mcCtrl_one_pauliXGate_eq_cnotGate`. -/
theorem tensorPowMcCtrlX_one_eq_congr_cnotGate :
    Evolution.tensorPowMcCtrlX 1 = Evolution.congr (qtowerQubitTensorPow 1) cnotGate := by
  rw [Evolution.tensorPowMcCtrlX_def, mcCtrl_one_pauliXGate_eq_cnotGate]

/-- **The symmetric-register `C²(X)` block is the named `Toffoli`.** The two-control block
`Evolution.tensorPowMcCtrlX 2` on `qubit ^⊗ₛ 3` is the named Toffoli gate transported along the
tower ↔ tensor-power bridge:
`tensorPowMcCtrlX 2 = Evolution.congr (qtowerQubitTensorPow 2) toffoliGate`. From
`tensorPowMcCtrlX_def` and `mcCtrl_two_pauliXGate_eq_toffoliGate`. -/
theorem tensorPowMcCtrlX_two_eq_congr_toffoliGate :
    Evolution.tensorPowMcCtrlX 2 = Evolution.congr (qtowerQubitTensorPow 2) toffoliGate := by
  rw [Evolution.tensorPowMcCtrlX_def, mcCtrl_two_pauliXGate_eq_toffoliGate]

/-- **The wire-placed `C⁰(X)` block is the named `NOT` placed on wires.** The exact form
`placedMcNot` uses for a `|S| = 0` gate: `Evolution.placedMcCtrlX 0 b σ` is the transported named
`NOT` gate placed on the `σ`-image wires,
`(Evolution.congr (qtowerQubitTensorPow 0) pauliXGate).onWires b σ`. From `placedMcCtrlX_def` and
`tensorPowMcCtrlX_zero_eq_congr_pauliXGate`. -/
theorem placedMcCtrlX_zero_eq_onWires_pauliXGate (b : ℕ) (σ : Equiv.Perm (Fin (0 + 1 + b))) :
    Evolution.placedMcCtrlX 0 b σ
      = (Evolution.congr (qtowerQubitTensorPow 0) pauliXGate).onWires b σ := by
  rw [Evolution.placedMcCtrlX_def, tensorPowMcCtrlX_zero_eq_congr_pauliXGate]

/-- **The wire-placed `C¹(X)` block is the named `CNOT` placed on wires.** The exact form
`placedMcNot` uses for a `|S| = 1` gate: `Evolution.placedMcCtrlX 1 b σ` is the transported named
`CNOT` gate placed on the `σ`-image wires,
`(Evolution.congr (qtowerQubitTensorPow 1) cnotGate).onWires b σ`. From `placedMcCtrlX_def` and
`tensorPowMcCtrlX_one_eq_congr_cnotGate`. -/
theorem placedMcCtrlX_one_eq_onWires_cnotGate (b : ℕ) (σ : Equiv.Perm (Fin (1 + 1 + b))) :
    Evolution.placedMcCtrlX 1 b σ
      = (Evolution.congr (qtowerQubitTensorPow 1) cnotGate).onWires b σ := by
  rw [Evolution.placedMcCtrlX_def, tensorPowMcCtrlX_one_eq_congr_cnotGate]

/-- **The wire-placed `C²(X)` block is the named `Toffoli` placed on wires.** The exact form
`placedMcNot` uses for a `|S| = 2` gate: `Evolution.placedMcCtrlX 2 b σ` is the transported named
`Toffoli` gate placed on the `σ`-image wires,
`(Evolution.congr (qtowerQubitTensorPow 2) toffoliGate).onWires b σ`. From `placedMcCtrlX_def` and
`tensorPowMcCtrlX_two_eq_congr_toffoliGate`. -/
theorem placedMcCtrlX_two_eq_onWires_toffoliGate (b : ℕ) (σ : Equiv.Perm (Fin (2 + 1 + b))) :
    Evolution.placedMcCtrlX 2 b σ
      = (Evolution.congr (qtowerQubitTensorPow 2) toffoliGate).onWires b σ := by
  rw [Evolution.placedMcCtrlX_def, tensorPowMcCtrlX_two_eq_congr_toffoliGate]

end

end AxQM
